1740	    // doesn't hold the token can neither approve the tool nor burn the pending
1741	    // waiter. We peek under a read lock, constant-time-compare, and only remove
1742	    // the waiter once the token is proven. A waiter bound to a token
1743	    // (`Some`, the safe default for any client-submitted turn) REQUIRES a
1744	    // matching token; an unbound waiter (`None`, legacy/daemon-internal turn)
1745	    // skips the check so existing internal flows keep working.
