 797	/// Mint a fresh high-entropy per-turn permission `decision_token` (OCEAN-185).
 798	///
 799	/// Two v4 UUIDs (~244 bits of OS-seeded randomness), concatenated as hex. A
 800	/// client calls this once per turn, sends the value on the turn submission
 801	/// (`decision_token`), and replays the SAME value on any
 802	/// `/v1/permissions/{id}/decision` POST for that turn. The value travels only on
 803	/// the authenticated submit/decision request path the submitter holds — it is
 804	/// NEVER placed on the public `/v1/events` SSE — so an attacker who only sniffed
 805	/// the broadcast `permission_id` cannot forge an approval. Built on `uuid` (an
 806	/// existing dependency) to avoid pulling a fresh RNG crate; `Uuid::new_v4` draws
 807	/// from the OS CSPRNG via `getrandom`.
 808	pub fn mint_decision_token() -> String {
 809	    format!("{}{}", Uuid::new_v4().simple(), Uuid::new_v4().simple())
 810	}
